Q: result of sizeof expected expression on array declaration A: <p>The <em>expected expression</em> part tells me that something is probably going wrong inside the macro. Are you sure that you have not defined anything else named <em>drone</em> inside <code>drone.c</code> so that the compiler interprets <code>(drone*)</code> as a multiplication with nothing?</p>
<p>I get the exact same error as you if I for example put</p>
<pre><code>int drone;
static char result[DRONE_STATUS_LENGTH];
</code></pre>

Q: Codeigniter: forbidden, you don&#39;t have permission to access this resource. What exact resource is it referring.? A: <p>I had same error days ago. I had to use <code>base64_encode</code> on the user input before sending the post vars to the API REST</p>
<p>Here an example of what I refer</p>
<p>Before</p>
<pre><code>// Vars causing the issue
// User input from Text Area with CKEDITOR JS
$answ = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post(&quot;answ&quot;);
// User input. Just tetxtbox
$question = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post(&quot;question&quot;); 
</code></pre>
<p>After</p>
<pre><code>$answ = base64_encode($this-&gt;input-&gt;post(&quot;answ&quot;)); 
$question = base64_encode($this-&gt;input-&gt;post(&quot;question&quot;));
</code></pre>
<p>Then</p>
<pre><code>postVars = [
        'siteq'=&gt;$question, 
        'answ'=&gt;$answ
    ];
// Sending the postvars by my post method
</code></pre>
<p>It seems to be relationed to apache mod_security</p>
<p>Here you have some related questions</p>
<p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/32983394/12436158">https://stackoverflow.com/a/32983394/12436158</a></p>
<p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/14256141/12436158">https://stackoverflow.com/a/14256141/12436158</a></p>

Q: Sending Email Via Kotlin A: <p>When a few things are checked:</p>
<p>cannot have sendmail on main thread</p>
<pre><code>fun onClickBtn2(view: View){
    Toast.makeText(this@MainActivity, &quot;Button 2 was pressed.&quot;, Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show()

    val thread = Thread {
        try {
            val sender = GMailSender(
                &quot;Arnold.Schwarzenegger@gmail.com&quot;,
                &quot;gmail app pass word&quot;
            )

            val subject = &quot;oh my god&quot;
            val message = &quot;Herrgott&quot;
            val recipients = &quot;Plain@mydomain.com&quot;
            sender.sendMail(subject, message, &quot;Arnie.Bread&quot;, recipients)
        } catch (e: Exception) {
            e.printStackTrace()
        }
    }

    // Thread starten
    thread.start()
}
</code></pre>
<p>Syntax in gradle file has changed:</p>
<pre><code>implementation(&quot;com.sun.mail:android-mail:1.6.0&quot;)
implementation(&quot;com.sun.mail:android-activation:1.6.0&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p>Internet grant in Manifest File</p>
<pre><code> &lt;uses-permission android:name=&quot;android.permission.INTERNET&quot; /&gt;
</code></pre>
